/.well-known/security.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain

# The OCR sandbox (ADR-0028). Its own policy, deliberately different from the
# application's above — and the only place `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is permitted.
#
# The application origin must never have it: that origin holds the GitHub token and
# the BYOK AI key. This document holds nothing. It is embedded with
# `sandbox="allow-scripts"` and no `allow-same-origin`, so it runs on an opaque origin
# with no access to the app's storage, and `connect-src 'self'` lets it load its own
# model files and reach nothing else.
#
# `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` is not decoration — it *overrides* the `DENY` this path
# inherits from `/*`, and without it the sandbox cannot exist. Cloudflare applies every
# matching rule rather than the most specific one, and a block only overrides the
# headers it names, so `/ocr/index.html` was being served `DENY`: unframeable from
# anywhere, same-origin included. The 2026-09-14 spike reported nothing at all because
# the frame never loaded, which read exactly like a missing capability and was not one.
# `frame-ancestors 'self'` above is the modern control and is meant to supersede this
# header; a browser that honours both wins the argument, and one demonstrably did.
/ocr/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'; img-src blob: data:; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
